        <body>
            <div xml:id="d289">

                <pb facs="0395" n="277" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg277"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/26: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-06-11T10:00:00-00:44">June 11, 1929—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>17. Referring to Department’s telegram of June 5, 5 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >6</hi>] p.m. Note delivered to Secretary of State, June 10, 11 a.m.,<anchor
                        n="6" xml:id="d289-f1"/> who said: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“This is an old story. The Department does not say if the charges are
                            true but assumes that they are true. They are serious and we will
                            investigate but there being no specific instance charged investigation
                            may be difficult”.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Apparent that intention is to treat matter as a recurrence of the old charges of
                    slavery against Liberia. He referred to the charge of slavery made by League of
                    Nations. It is anticipated that his note in reply to mine will be a general
                    denial and only touch lightly on shipments to Fernando Po, in effect that only
                    those who volunteer are sent.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
